BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 269.77 Tm (The costliest buy-side failure is a choice problem dressed up as an integration problem. The POTOMAC M&A banker) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 254.55 Tm (walks through the case of Jennifer, who ran a $10M-revenue finance SaaS company and bought a competitor that a) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 239.32 Tm (banker pitched. The target was 70% of the size, 15 years older, slower-growing and on antiquated tech. Customers) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 224.10 Tm (refused to migrate because switching mission-critical software is expensive, and synergies dried up. Jennifer's team) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 208.88 Tm (held equity while the target's team had none, and the two collided, leaving 'two separate businesses under one umbrella') Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 193.65 Tm ([RLr8PdCZ6U0 @ 00:11:25]. The same banker flags the quiet margin killer: paying $15M where the business stands at) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 178.43 Tm ($10M means 'you've literally just paid the seller for the value creation' [RLr8PdCZ6U0 @ 00:41:11]. Money Sutra puts) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 163.20 Tm (the arithmetic bluntly. Deal value is standalone value plus credible synergies, minus fees, financing and integration) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 147.98 Tm (costs, and 'the buyer should not justify a deal using synergies alone' [aBB5nV2vr2Q @ 00:06:21]. Hacking the Case) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 132.75 Tm (Interview adds the check Jennifer skipped. If leaning no, look at alternative targets and opportunity cost, because 'the) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 117.53 Tm (money spent on making the acquisition could be spent on something else' [J1GpLqugFeM @ 00:06:01].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 102.30 Tm (On the sell side, the traps cluster around the LOI. The POTOMAC M&A banker warns that the LOI ends competition) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 87.08 Tm (through exclusivity, a no-shop clause and a notice duty. Escrow, R&W insurance, caps and baskets therefore must be) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 71.85 Tm (locked inside it; leave them open and expect a buyer to come back demanding a '$2 million' escrow once rivals are) Tj ET
