BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 716.00 Tm (gone [8jBQ3jZnNvY @ 01:05:02]. The buy-side session confirms the flip from the other chair: the buyer's LOI is one) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 700.77 Tm (page with long exclusivity, and leverage shifts to the buyer the moment it is signed [RLr8PdCZ6U0 @ 00:46:13]. The) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 685.55 Tm (biggest mid-market deal killer is not price but seller emotion, and the remedy taught is emotional reappraisal. Repeated) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 670.32 Tm (deadline slippage destroys credibility too, because 'people do not like to make decisions under time pressure') Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 655.10 Tm ([f7d2hP31YB8 @ 00:16:52]. Pietro Conte adds the speed tax: 'If the process ever is slowed up by the investment bank,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 639.87 Tm (time just does weird things to deal.' That is why diligence answers go back by 9:00 a.m., so management keeps running) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 624.65 Tm (the business. It is also why overselling backfires, as when drawers were pitched as 'highly engineered linear movement) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 609.42 Tm (solutions' [1PBrwvp_6us @ 00:14:16].) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 594.20 Tm (The economics checks start with the adviser's bill. Saverio Canepa runs two proposals at the same 2% on a ?10M) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 578.97 Tm (enterprise value with ?2M net debt. Taking 2% of the ?8M equity value, with a credited ?20K retainer, costs ?160K.) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 563.75 Tm (Taking 2% of enterprise value, with an uncredited retainer, costs ?220K: a ?60K gap where 'the percentage is identical.') Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 548.52 Tm (Canepa's checklist then asks which event triggers the fee, how deferred or reinvested consideration enters the base,) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 533.30 Tm (what stays due if the deal dies, and how long the tail runs [kIcxjlHfa74 @ 00:01:46]. Michael Wildeveld warns that) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 518.07 Tm (some M&A advisors sign undersized clients just to collect $5-15K upfront fees. Mid-market and bank retainers can run) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 502.85 Tm ($150-250K or more, and Goldman Sachs-type banks are not worth the fees on small deals [Dx_mEuS7ipk @) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 487.62 Tm (00:04:37]. Simple Explain flags the incentive cost of percentage ladders like the 5-4-3-2-1% Lehman formula:) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 472.40 Tm (short-term focus, conflicts of interest and excessive risk-taking [vTGW5-gVWNY @ 00:01:28]. On earnouts, Canepa) Tj ET
BT /F1 10.5 Tf 1 0 0 1 54.00 457.17 Tm (warns that staying with the business does not guarantee control. A payment guarantee 'cannot ensure that performance) Tj ET
